To create a pop-up that resembles a virus alert to educate you about potential online scams, follow these steps:

1. Create a new HTML file: Open a text editor or code editor and create a new file. Save it with a .html extension.

2. Add HTML tags: In the new file, add the necessary HTML tags to create a pop-up window. Here's an example:
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <title>Virus Alert</title>
  <style>
    body {
      background-color: #f0f0f0;
      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
      font-size: 14px;
      color: #333;
    }
    h1 {
      color: #f00;
    }
    .popup {
      display: none;
      position: fixed;
      top: 50%;
      left: 50%;
      transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
      background-color: #fff;
      border: 1px solid #888;
      padding: 20px;
      z-index: 999;
    }
    .popup.show {
      display: block;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>Virus Alert</h1>
  <p>You are at risk of falling victim to online scams. Be cautious and aware of potential threats. 
    <a href="#" class="close">Close</a>
  </p>
</body>
</html>
```
1. Add JavaScript code: In the same file, add JavaScript code to create the pop-up window. Here's an example:
```javascript
function showPopup() {
  var popup = document.getElementById("popup");
  popup.classList.add("show");
}

function closePopup() {
  var popup = document.getElementById("popup");
  popup.classList.remove("show");
}

var closeButton = document.querySelector(".close");
closeButton.addEventListener("click", closePopup);

